course: dictionary
lesson: 3598
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fierceness is a noun, a name for a thing or a quality. It comes from the word fierce. Many words have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it, then try each meaning in the sentence.
explain: «The fierceness of the storm knocked down trees.» Here fierceness means very great strength or force. Nothing in the sentence says the storm was angry, so we do not need the meaning about wild, angry animals.
explain: «The tiger's fierceness made the hunters step back.» Here fierceness means being wild, angry and ready to attack, like a fierce animal. The clues are the tiger and the hunters stepping back.
explain: «That fierceness has a good side — she is brave, loyal and never boring — and a hard side: it gets her into fights.» This sentence is about strong feeling and character. Fierceness can be a good quality, such as loyalty, but it can also cause trouble.
fact: Fierceness means being wild, angry and ready to attack, like a fierce animal.
fact: Fierceness can also mean very great strength or force, such as of a storm, fire or competition.
fact: Fierceness can mean strong, passionate feeling, such as fierce love or loyalty.
fact: «Fierce» is the root word, so if you know fierce, you can often work out fierceness.
exercise: «The fierceness of the storm knocked down trees.» What does fierceness mean here? | A gentle, calm feeling | *Very great strength or force | A cold and dark morning | Wild and ready to attack, like an animal
exercise: «The lioness showed her fierceness when the cubs were in danger.» What does fierceness mean here? | Sadness and tiredness | Very great strength of a storm | *Wild, angry and ready to attack | Being very quick to laugh
exercise: «That fierceness has a good side — she is brave, loyal and never boring.» What does fierceness describe? | Being very small | A rainy, grey day | A broken window | *Strong, passionate feeling and loyalty
test: Fierceness is which part of speech? | Adverb | *Noun | Verb | Adjective
test: Which phrase uses fierceness to mean great force? | a sleepy cat | a gentle breeze | a happy song | *the fierceness of the storm
exam: Which sentence shows fierceness as strong, passionate loyalty? | The fierceness of the morning fog hid the hills. | The storm's fierceness knocked the fence flat. | The wolf's fierceness scared the hikers off the path. | *She defended her best friend with fierceness and never gave up on him.
